          <li><a href="#signature-specs">Signature Specifications</a></li>
          <li><a href="#step-by-step">Step-by-Step Preparation</a></li>
          <li><a href="#rejections">Common Rejection Reasons</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 id="live-vs-scan">Live Capture vs. Scanned Upload</h2>

      <p>SSC CGL 2026 now requires live photo capture through the portal in addition to a scanned photo upload. The live capture verifies you're a real applicant at the time of registration. The scanned upload is what appears on your admit card and application form, so it still needs to meet the exact file specs below.</p>

      <h2 id="photo-specs">Photo Specifications</h2>

      <p>Photo must be <strong>200×230 pixels</strong>, <a href="/compress/to-50kb">20–50KB</a>, JPEG/JPG only. Requirements:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>White background, recent colour passport-style photo</li>
        <li>No spectacles, no caps</li>
        <li>Applies across CGL, CHSL, MTS, GD, CPO, and Stenographer exams</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="signature-specs">Signature Specifications</h2>

      <p>Signature must be <a href="/compress/to-20kb">10–20KB</a>, JPEG/JPG, approximately 4.0cm(w) × 2.0cm(h). A few things trip candidates up here:</p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p><strong>Running handwriting only.</strong> Capital-letter signatures are rejected. Your signature must be in running (cursive) handwriting, in black ink, on white unruled paper, filling at least 80% of the box.</p>
        <p><strong>Conflicting notification info.</strong> SSC's own CGL 2026 notification contains conflicting dimension info for signatures — 6×2cm in one section, 4×2cm in another. The safe approach is to follow the dimensions shown on the live upload interface itself, not just the PDF notification.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="step-by-step">Step-by-Step Preparation</h2>

      <ol>
        <li><strong>Resize</strong> your photo to 200×230px using the <a href="/resize/for-ssc">SSC resize tool</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Compress</strong> the photo to 20–50KB using the <a href="/compress/for-ssc">SSC compress tool</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Compress your signature</strong> to 10–20KB using the <a href="/compress/signature">signature compress tool</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Convert to JPEG</strong> if your files are PNG or HEIC, using the <a href="/convert/png-to-jpg">PNG to JPG converter</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Strip metadata</strong> before uploading identity-linked files, using the <a href="/metadata/remover">metadata remover</a>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="rejections">Common Rejection Reasons</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Blurred or illegible signature after over-compression</li>
        <li>Signature too small within the box (under 80% fill)</li>
        <li>Signature written in capital letters instead of running handwriting</li>
        <li>Spectacles visible in the photo</li>
        <li>Wrong pixel dimensions despite correct file size</li>
        <li>File too large for the portal's upload limit</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-[14px]">Specifications listed here are based on publicly available information as of 2026. Always verify the current requirements from the official exam notification before uploading.</p>

    </div>
